    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Canyon-TX/Assistant-Director-of-Student-Engagement---Belonging_R-095419-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Engagement & Belonging",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Director of Student Engagement & Belonging Agency West Texas A&M University Department Student Engagement And Leadership Proposed Minimum Salary $3,555.50 monthly Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. General Summary: The Assistant Director of Student Activities provides strategic leadership for campus-wide engagement initiatives that foster student connection, leadership development, community engagement, and a sense of belonging. Through innovative programming, leadership education, service opportunities, and assessment practices, this position creates meaningful pathways for students to engage in campus life and enhance their overall student experience.  The Assistant Director advises the Campus Activities Board (CAB), develops and facilitates leadership development initiatives, coordinates community engagement and service opportunities, and collaborates with campus partners to advance institutional goals related to student engagement, belonging, retention, and student success. Responsibilities: Conducts planning, organizing, and executing events on various scales and types (campus traditions, leadership development, community service, etc.). This includes coordinating logistics, managing budgets, securing venues, negotiating contracts, risk management, curriculum, marketing, assessment, and overall smooth event operations. Directly supervises approximately 5 Student Consultants and an additional group of 25-75 students who volunteer in the capacity of planning and facilitating campus events. Create, maintain, and promote programming and activities calendar with special attention to student organization engagement opportunities. Collaborate with ongoing co-curricular partnerships with academic leaders that result in cross-divisional and cross-institutional student learning outcomes. Engage in marketing and promotional efforts including presentations that promote and encourage student engagement. Conduct assessments to implement best practice methods for event planning, membership development, leadership curriculum, service opportunities, recruitment, budget development and program effectiveness. Handling email communication, phone calls, other inquiries related to student activities, events, leadership development and community service opportunities. Work nights and weekends as needed. Maintains 100% compliance with timely completion of required System, University and job-specific online training courses. This document represents the major duties, responsibilities, and authorities of this job, and is not intended to be a complete list of all tasks and functions.  Other duties as assigned. Necessary Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in related field or combination of education and experience. Four (4) years of professional experience in management of Student Activities programs. Experience planning and facilitating campus-wide events, Homecoming and Welcome Week activities, leadership training, and community service activities. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills, analytical, critical thinking, and organizational skills, ability to work in a high energy, flexible team environment. Planning large-scale campus events, advising students, collaborating with campus and community partners. Administrative skills, event planning skills, prioritization skills are necessary. Experience with marketing and promotional effort related to growth in student activity participation. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s Degree in higher education, student affairs, marketing, or related field. Five (5) years of related experience in management of Student Activities programs contributing to significant student engagement efforts/initiatives. Experience advising/supervising student staff and providing professional development. Utilizing assessments to make data informed decisions. Ability to develop collaborative partnerships with campus and community stakeholders. Knowledge and experience working with Student Activities programs, student organizations, campus engagement. Knowledge and understanding of student development theory, student personnel administration, and retention. Has experience creating and facilitating broad engagement, socialization, and student development through the delivery of a dynamic calendar of on and off-campus events for a variety of student populations. Manage programming budget, goals, processes, assessment regarding campus programs, leadership and service events. Applicant Instructions: Please include the following with your application: Cover letter Resume Three references Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the “My Experience” page before continuing through the application.  Please use the “Upload” button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.  If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. Texas law requires all males age 18 through 25 to be properly registered with the Selective Service System. Equal Opportunity /Veterans/Disability Employer.  All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Canyon-TX/Philanthropy-System-Analyst_R-095410-1": {
      "title": "Philanthropy System Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Philanthropy System Analyst Agency West Texas A&M University Department Advancement Services Proposed Minimum Salary $4,072.25 monthly Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits   NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval.   General Summary:   The Philanthropy System Analyst is responsible for working with others in all areas of the Philanthropy Division as well as with IT to identify operational problems and find solutions. The Philanthropy System Analyst will train users, create reports, conduct user acceptance testing and assist the Philanthropy Team to use the Philanthropy System so it provides the greatest ROI. Responsibilities: Create lists, queries and exports to extract data from the Ascend CRM with specific criteria Work with IT to develop Ascend CRM to meet the needs of philanthropy users and IT Provide user support for Ascend CRM functionality. Test new releases/updates and work with Philanthropy leadership in decision making and implementation of changes. Develop and recommend data integrity and quality audits for the Ascend CRM to ensure the accuracy of data entry and record coding. Develop methods for streamlining data entry and extraction processes within Ascend CRM. Develop and document relevant business processes involving Ascend CRM including a data dictionary, code tables and crosswalks for data that exists across multiple systems Performs regular data appending procedures from a variety of sources (example: NCOA update and email appends, etc.) following best practices Work with Alumni and Annual Giving on appeal standards, tracking appeal performance, etc. This document represents the major duties, responsibilities, and authorities of this job and is not intended to be a complete list of all tasks and functions. Other duties as assigned. Maintains 100% compliance with timely completion of required System, University and job-specific online training courses. Necessary Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. Four (4) years of related experience. Systems Analyst experience. Working with end users and IT. Knowledge of donor software (example: Raisers Edge, Ascend, Salesforce, etc.). Create lists, queries and exports. Understanding of data administration and management functions. Proficiency in Microsoft Office primary software, particularly Excel for use with data. Ability to train, motivate and communicate with staff in a high-volume goal oriented, friendly work environment. Ability to maintain confidentiality. Ability to learn and effectively use new software. Self-Motivated, self-directed, collegial, creative and results oriented. Must have an advanced ability to prioritize tasks, schedules and objectives. Must be collaborative with a strong commitment to team support and positive customer service. Excellent written and verbal communication skills along with strong interpersonal skills and attention to detail. Technical understanding of CRM database systems. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in computer science or related management field. Eight (8) years of related experience. Experience in developing and maintaining dashboards for displaying and analyzing data. Experience with Ascend, Affinaquest, Salesforce and/or Raisers Edge. Fundraising CRM experience.   Applicant Instructions: Please include the following with your application: Cover letter Resume Three references Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the “My Experience” page before continuing through the application.  Please use the “Upload” button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.  If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. Texas law requires all males age 18 through 25 to be properly registered with the Selective Service System. Equal Opportunity /Veterans/Disability Employer.  All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Canyon-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Health-Sciences_R-095062-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Health Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Health Sciences Agency West Texas A&M University Department Sports And Exercise Science Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. Job Summary: The Health Science Faculty at West Texas A&M University is responsible for delivering high-quality instruction, supporting student success, and contributing to the growth and development of the Health Science Department. This position involves teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses, developing and revising curriculum, and engaging in service activities that support the mission of the university and the healthcare workforce needs of the Texas Panhandle. The instructor will provide engaging, evidence-based instruction in areas such as population health, healthcare systems, health promotion, and rural health, utilizing a variety of instructional modalities including face-to-face, hybrid, and online delivery. The role includes mentoring students, advising on academic and career pathways, and facilitating experiential learning opportunities such as internships, clinical placements, and community-based projects. In addition to teaching responsibilities, the Health Science Instructor will participate in program assessment, accreditation activities, and continuous quality improvement initiatives. The position requires collaboration with faculty, staff, and community partners to strengthen healthcare education pathways and expand workforce development efforts. The ideal candidate demonstrates a commitment to academic excellence, student-centered learning, and service to rural and underserved populations. This role supports the broader mission of West Texas A&M University by preparing graduates who are equipped to meet the evolving healthcare needs of the region and beyond. Work Performed: The Health Science Faculty at West Texas A&M University performs a broad range of teaching, service, and program development responsibilities that support the mission of the College of Nursing and Health Sciences and the University's commitment to preparing healthcare professionals who improve the health and well-being of the Texas Panhandle and beyond. The College emphasizes developing exemplary practitioners through education, research, service, outreach, and community partnerships. Primary responsibilities include planning, developing, and delivering undergraduate and graduate Health Science courses using evidence-based instructional practices in face-to-face, hybrid, and online learning environments. The instructor evaluates student learning outcomes, maintains academic records, provides academic advising and mentoring, and fosters an inclusive learning environment that promotes student engagement, retention, persistence, and graduation. Necessary Qualifications: Masters or Doctoral degree (PhD, DrPH, EdD, DNP, or related) in Health Sciences, Public Health, Healthcare Administration, or a closely related field from an accredited institution Demonstrated teaching effectiveness in undergraduate and/or graduate health science courses (face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online formats) Evidence of expertise in one or more relevant areas such as population health, rural health, healthcare systems, epidemiology, health promotion, or health policy Strong communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to engage diverse student populations Commitment to student success, mentorship, and experiential learning (internships, clinicals, or applied practice experiences) Ability to contribute to curriculum development, program assessment, and continuous quality improvement Demonstrated organizational and leadership skills to support program growth and community engagement Eligibility for appointment consistent with university and system policies Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree (PhD, DrPH, EdD, DNP, or related) in Health Sciences. Experience teaching in a rural-serving or regional university environment with a demonstrated record of scholarship, research, or creative activity appropriate to rank (publications, presentations, grant activity) Experience with accreditation processes (e.g., program review, outcomes assessment, compliance reporting) Established relationships or experience working with healthcare systems, public health agencies, or community organizations Experience securing or participating in grant-funded projects or workforce development initiatives Interdisciplinary collaboration experience across health-related programs Experience with student advising, retention initiatives, and career placement support Professional certification or licensure relevant to the discipline (e.g., CHES, MHA, RN, APRN, etc.), if applicable Applicant Instructions:   We require the following:  Letter of interest or cover letter Curriculum Vitae Portfolio of creative work (where applicable) Personal statement to include philosophy and plans for research, teaching and service, as applicable Samples of unpublished works or works in progress (where applicable) Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts are expected to be submitted promptly by the successful candidate) Three professional references Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the “My Experience” page before continuing through the application.  Please use the “Upload” button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.  If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . Texas law requires that males age 18 through 25 be properly registered with the Selective Service System in order to be eligible for employment. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits All applicants must attest they are not employed by and do not have any connection or continuous connections to any government entity or political apparatus of a country listed in 15 C.F.R. § 791.4. Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. For additional questions or information regarding this position, please contact: Search Committee Chair: Michelle Kirksey        Department: College of Nursing and Health Sciences Phone: (806) 651-2693 Email: mkirksey@wtamu.edu All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Canyon-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Agricultural-Business-Economics_R-094880-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Agricultural Business/Economics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Agricultural Business/Economics Agency West Texas A&M University Department Agricultural Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. Job Summary: West Texas A&M University, a member of The Texas A&M University System, invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Agricultural Business and Economics. This is a nine-month, tenure track position that reports to the Head of the Department of Agricultural Sciences. WTAMU is located in the Texas Panhandle, one of the largest cattle feeding areas in the world (6 million head annually), and one of the most prolific crop-producing areas in the world, (14 million acres of cultivated cropland), both of which are multi-billion dollars industries. The highest total value crops in the region are wheat, corn, ensilage, hay, sorghum and cotton. The position will focus on the various aspects of agricultural economics including but not limited to management, marketing, finance, policy, trade, and retail sales and will provide support to the current academic track to increase the enrollment at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. WTAMU is a four-year academic institution with more than 9,000 students including more than 1,150 students in the department granting Bachelor, Master of Science, Master of Agriculture, and Doctoral degrees. The department offers the following degrees related to the discipline: B.S. degree in Agribusiness, B.S. degree in Agricultural Business and Economics, M.S. in Agriculture with an emphasis in Agricultural Business and Economics, M.Ag, and a Ph.D. in Systems Agriculture. Work Performed:  Teach a minimum of 9 hours per long semester. Teaching opportunities may include face-to-face and/or online formats. Contribute to a strong teaching program in the agricultural economics/agribusiness area with emphasis in at least one of the following areas: production and resource management, finance, international trade, policy, or management. Develop a research program in an area of agricultural economics/agribusiness. Secure extramural funding for research and scholarly activities. Advise M.S. and Ph.D. graduate students in various areas of Agricultural Business and Economics. Publish research findings and syntheses in refereed journals. Develop collaborative programs with scientists in other agencies, universities, and the agriculture industry. Develop strong industry relationships with agribusiness professionals in the region/state. Foster employment opportunities for both undergraduate and graduate students. Other duties as assigned. Necessary Qualifications: Ph.D. in Agricultural Economics, Economics, Agribusiness or closely related field Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching, research, and service Working knowledge and experience in crop and livestock industries Academic or industry experience beyond the Ph.D. is preferred Commitment to an interdisciplinary team approach to education and research Interpersonal skills, and desire to establish working relationships with external constituents in the allied agriculture industries Demonstrated experience in securing external funding and scholarly publication Excellent written and oral communication skills Applicant Instructions:   We require the following:  Letter of interest or cover letter Curriculum Vitae Portfolio of creative work (where applicable) Personal statement to include philosophy and plans for research, teaching and service, as applicable Samples of unpublished works or works in progress (where applicable) Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts are expected to be submitted promptly by the successful candidate) Three professional references Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the “My Experience” page before continuing through the application.  Please use the “Upload” button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.  If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . Texas law requires that males age 18 through 25 be properly registered with the Selective Service System in order to be eligible for employment. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits All applicants must attest they are not employed by and do not have any connection or continuous connections to any government entity or political apparatus of a country listed in 15 C.F.R. § 791.4. Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. For additional questions or information regarding this position, please contact: Search Committee Chair:  Dr. Bridget Guerrero Department:  Agricultural Sciences Phone:   (806) 651-2614 Email:   bguerrero@wtamu.edu All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Canyon-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Accounting_R-093554-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Accounting Agency West Texas A&M University Department Accounting, Economics & Finance Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. Teach undergraduate and/or graduate accounting courses, advise and mentor students, develop curriculum, and actively engage in scholarly research. Maintain professional knowledge, contribute to service activities in the department and college, and participate in ongoing professional development. Requires a doctorate (or master’s for certain positions), demonstrated teaching ability, research record, and strong communication skills. Professional certification (e.g., CPA) is preferred. Work Performed:  In a faculty position in accounting, the primary responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and/or graduate accounting courses, developing and updating course materials, advising and mentoring students, and assessing student learning. The faculty member will also conduct research in the field of accounting, publish scholarly work, participate in departmental and university service such as committees and curriculum development, and stay current with changes in accounting standards and educational practices. Additionally, they may collaborate with industry and professional organizations to ensure coursework remains relevant and support student career development. Necessary Qualifications: Applicants for the accounting faculty position must hold a doctorate (PHD DBA) in accounting or a closely related field from an accredited institution; The candidate should have demonstrated effectiveness in university-level teaching and a documented record of scholarly research or clear potential for research productivity in accounting or a related area. Strong oral and written communication skills, the ability to mentor students, and a commitment to foster diversity and inclusion are required. Preferred Qualifications: Professional certifications such as CPA or CMA, experience with accounting software and technology, previous university teaching experience, curriculum development expertise, and proficiency in online or hybrid instruction are strongly preferred. Applicant Instructions:   We require the following:  Letter of interest or cover letter Curriculum Vitae Portfolio of creative work (where applicable) Personal statement to include philosophy and plans for research, teaching and service, as applicable Samples of unpublished works or works in progress (where applicable) Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts are expected to be submitted promptly by the successful candidate) Three professional references Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the “My Experience” page before continuing through the application.  Please use the “Upload” button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.  If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . Texas law requires that males age 18 through 25 be properly registered with the Selective Service System in order to be eligible for employment. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits All applicants must attest they are not employed by and do not have any connection or continuous connections to any government entity or political apparatus of a country listed in 15 C.F.R. § 791.4. Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
